    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-sexual-conduct-act-1994-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Arbitrary interferences with privacy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-sexual-conduct-act-1994#sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-sexual-conduct-act-1994.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-sexual-conduct-act-1994.pdf, p.5",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sexual conduct involving only consenting adults acting in private\nis not to be subject, by or under any law of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory, to any arbitrary interference with privacy\nwithin the meaning of Article 17 of the International Covenant on\nCivil and Political Rights.\nNote:\nArticle 17 of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights\nis set out in Schedule 2 to the Australian Human Rights Commission\nAct 1986.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this section, an adult is a person who is 18\nyears old or more.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2009C00395\n\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2009C00395\n\n\nNotes to the  Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994\n\nTable of Acts\n\nHuman Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994                    3\nNotes to the Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act\nNote 1\nThe Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994 as shown in this compilation\ncomprises Act No. 179, 1994 amended as indicated in the Tables below.\nTable of Acts\nAct\nNumber\nand year\nDate\nof Assent\nDate of\ncommencement\nApplication,\nsaving or\ntransitional\nprovisions\nHuman Rights (Sexual\nConduct) Act 1994\n179, 1994",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sexual conduct involving only consenting adults acting in private\nis not to be subject, by or under any law of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory, to any arbitrary interference with privacy\nwithin the meaning of Article 17 of the International Covenant on\nCivil and Political Rights.\nNote:\nArticle 17 of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights\nis set out in Schedule 2 to the Australian Human Rights Commission\nAct 1986.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this section, an adult is a person who is 18\nyears old or more.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2009C00395\n\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2009C00395\n\n\nNotes to the  Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994\n\nTable of Acts\n\nHuman Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994                    3\nNotes to the Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act\nNote 1\nThe Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994 as shown in this compilation\ncomprises Act No. 179, 1994 amended as indicated in the Tables below.\nTable of Acts\nAct\nNumber\nand year\nDate\nof Assent\nDate of\ncommencement\nApplication,\nsaving or\ntransitional\nprovisions\nHuman Rights (Sexual\nConduct) Act 1994\n179, 1994",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-sexual-conduct-act-1994-sec-4-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-sexual-conduct-act-1994-sec-4-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "700128c3b60146a6730b3df4728bdd84208e6dc081e70382dd9a06a7f47e565c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-sexual-conduct-act-1994#sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Arbitrary interferences with privacy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 5,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sexual conduct involving only consenting adults acting in private\nis not to be subject, by or under any law of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory, to any arbitrary interference with privacy\nwithin the meaning of Article 17 of the International Covenant on\nCivil and Political Rights.\nNote:\nArticle 17 of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights\nis set out in Schedule 2 to the Australian Human Rights Commission\nAct 1986.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this section, an adult is a person who is 18\nyears old or more.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2009C00395\n\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2009C00395\n\n\nNotes to the  Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994\n\nTable of Acts\n\nHuman Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994                    3\nNotes to the Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act\nNote 1\nThe Human Rights (Sexual Conduct) Act 1994 as shown in this compilation\ncomprises Act No. 179, 1994 amended as indicated in the Tables below.\nTable of Acts\nAct\nNumber\nand year\nDate\nof Assent\nDate of\ncommencement\nApplication,\nsaving or\ntransitional\nprovisions\nHuman Rights (Sexual\nConduct) Act 1994\n179, 1994"
